[style name="DefaultStyle"]
*ring ring*
do StateManager.checkState("trail1GoLeft")
if {stateTemp} == true:
	Chencho (Default): Alright where to next? Right?
	Chud (Default): If I remember correctly, you should take the path to the left.
	Chencho (Happy): Bet.
	[style name="DefaultStyle"]
	CHOOSE A PATH
	- LEFT
		do StateManager.updateState("trail2GoLeft")
	- RIGHT
		do StateManager.updateState("trail2GoRight")
	do StateManager.checkState("trail2GoLeft")
	if {stateTemp} == true:
		Chencho (Upset): Bro, where did you send me?
		Chud (Worried): Uh… my bad man, I meant go right
		Chencho (Tired): Are you kidding me?
		Chud (Angry): What? It’s not like I’m leading you to hell. Just keep walking.
	do StateManager.checkState("trail2GoRight")
	if {stateTemp} == true:
		Chencho (Happy): Wow! You sure know how to pick hiking trails. This place is beautiful.
		Chud (Happy): Hehe, I know… I-I walked through there.
do StateManager.checkState("trail1GoRight")
if {stateTemp} == true:
	Chencho (Tired): Ok man, tell me which way to go. And you better be right this time.
	Chud (Default): I’m pretty sure you should go left.
	Chencho (Upset): What do you mean pretty sure? Are you fully sure?
	Chud (Worried): Uh… yea.
	[style name="DefaultStyle"]
	CHOOSE A PATH\:
	- Left
		do StateManager.updateState("trail2GoLeft")
	- Right
		do StateManager.updateState("trail2GoRight")
	do StateManager.checkState("trail2GoLeft")
	if {stateTemp} == true:
		Chencho (Upset): Dude you sure you’re not dyslexic? I think I’m still on the wrong path.
		Chud: Umm… Might be a possibility.
	do StateManager.checkState("trail2GoRight")
	if {stateTemp} == true:
		Chencho (Default): Ok, I think I’m on the right track again. This looks much better.
		Chud (Default): See, I told you.